{"name":"Wine Cellar","hex":"#70403d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wine cellar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An underground place for storing wine at a constant temperature.","A collection of wines."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine_cellar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wine cellar","blocks":[{"text":"A wine cellar is a storage room for wine in bottles or barrels, or more rarely in carboys, amphorae, or plastic containers. In an active wine cellar, important factors such as temperature and humidity are maintained by a climate control system. In contrast, passive wine cellars are not climate-controlled, and are usually built underground to reduce temperature swings. An aboveground wine cellar is often called a wine room, while a small wine cellar is sometimes termed a wine closet. The household department responsible for the storage, care and service of wine in a great mediaeval house was termed the buttery. Large wine cellars date back over 3,700 years."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Wine_cellar.jpg/330px-Wine_cellar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_cellar"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine"},{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Sonoma_Wine_Cellar-9462.jpg/120px-Sonoma_Wine_Cellar-9462.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Sonoma_Wine_Cellar-9462.jpg/250px-Sonoma_Wine_Cellar-9462.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Sonoma_Wine_Cellar-9462.jpg/120px-Sonoma_Wine_Cellar-9462.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASonoma_Wine_Cellar-9462.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Oxford_-_Jesus_College_-_0531.jpg/120px-Oxford_-_Jesus_College_-_0531.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Oxford_-_Jesus_College_-_0531.jpg/250px-Oxford_-_Jesus_College_-_0531.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Oxford_-_Jesus_College_-_0531.jpg/120px-Oxford_-_Jesus_College_-_0531.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOxford_-_Jesus_College_-_0531.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Muga_Wine_cellar.jpg/120px-Muga_Wine_cellar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Muga_Wine_cellar.jpg/250px-Muga_Wine_cellar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_